DOCUMENT 01 · DATABASE DESIGN AND MODELLING

Project Title: Design and Modelling of a Hospital/Clinic Management Database System

Selected Organisation: PrimeCare Hospital

1. Organisation Background

PrimeCare Hospital is a fictional healthcare institution established to provide medical services to individuals and families. The hospital offers healthcare services such as patient consultations, medical diagnosis, treatment, prescription administration and laboratory investigations.

The hospital attends to different categories of patients and maintains records of their personal information, medical consultations, appointments, prescriptions and laboratory results.

To improve the management of its daily operations, the hospital requires a centralised database system that will allow authorised healthcare personnel to store, manage, update and retrieve patient-related information efficiently.
2. Nature of Business / System
PrimeCare Hospital operates within the healthcare sector, providing medical consultations, diagnosis, treatment and laboratory services.

The proposed Hospital Management Database System will support the hospital's daily activities by providing a structured platform for managing patient information and medical records.

The system will manage the following activities:
- Patient registration and record management.
- Doctor information and specialisations.
- Appointment scheduling and management.
- Medical diagnosis recording.
- Prescription management.
- Laboratory investigation and result management.
- Retrieval of patients' medical histories.
3. Database Users

The proposed database system will be accessed by different categories of authorised users.
Database user	Responsibilities
Administrator	Manages database records and user access.
Doctors	Access patient records, record diagnoses and prescribe medication.
Nurses	Assist with patient information and appointment records.
Receptionists	Register patients and schedule appointments.
Laboratory personnel	Record laboratory investigations and test results.
Pharmacists	Access and manage prescription information.

4. Major Data Stored

The database will store the following categories of information:
Data category	Information stored
Patient records	Patient ID, name, date of birth, gender, address and contact details.
Doctor records	Doctor ID, name, speciality and contact information.
Appointment records	Appointment ID, patient ID, doctor ID, date, time and status.
Diagnosis records	Diagnosis ID, patient ID, doctor ID, diagnosis description and date.
Prescription records	Prescription ID, patient ID, doctor ID, medication, dosage and date.
Laboratory records	Laboratory ID, patient ID, test type, test result and date.

5. Key Database Operations

The proposed database system will support the following operations:
1. Patient registration: Register new patients and store their personal information.
2. Appointment booking: Schedule appointments between patients and doctors.
3. Doctor assignment: Associate appointments with the appropriate doctors.
4. Diagnosis management: Record and retrieve medical diagnoses.
5. Prescription management: Store and retrieve prescriptions issued by doctors.
6. Laboratory management: Record laboratory investigations and their results.
7. Medical history retrieval: Retrieve patients' previous appointments, diagnoses, prescriptions and laboratory records.
